{{also|Boer}}
==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Nl-boer.ogg|audio}}

===Etymology 1===
A short form of ''geboer'', which is a [[West Frisian]] or Eastern Dutch form of {{term|gebuur|lang=nl}}, which is cognate with Old English {{term|ġebūr|lang=ang}}.

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|g=m|boeren|boertje}}

# [[farmer]], [[peasant]]
# [[boor]], ruffian, yokel etc.
# '''-boer''' (''in compounds'') [[merchant]] (and sometimes producer) of a certain product group, mainly foods, often named after it, e.g. [[melkboer]] 'milkman'
# {{slang}} [[jack]] (playing cards)

=====Synonyms=====
* (''farmer'') [[landbouwer]] {{m}}, [[teler]] {{m}}, [[tuinder]] {{m}}, [[veehouder]] {{m}}

